     aauutthh__ddeessttrrooyy()            A function macro that destroys the authentica‐
                               tion information associated with _a_u_t_h.  De‐
                               struction usually involves deallocation of pri‐
                               vate data structures.  The use of _a_u_t_h is unde‐
                               fined after calling aauutthh__ddeessttrrooyy().

     aauutthhnnoonnee__ccrreeaattee()         Create and return an RPC authentication handle
                               that passes nonusable authentication informa‐
                               tion with each remote procedure call.  This is
                               the default authentication used by RPC.

     aauutthhssyyss__ccrreeaattee()          Create and return an RPC authentication handle
                               that contains AUTH_SYS authentication informa‐
                               tion.  The _h_o_s_t argument is the name of the ma‐
                               chine on which the information was created; _u_i_d
                               is the user's user ID; _g_i_d is the user's cur‐
                               rent group ID; _l_e_n and _a_u_p___g_i_d_s refer to a
                               counted array of groups to which the user be‐
                               longs.

     aauutthhssyyss__ccrreeaattee__ddeeffaauulltt()  Call aauutthhssyyss__ccrreeaattee() with the appropriate ar‐
                               guments.

